===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[sign#Noun|Signs]], particularly those [[impart]]ing [[commercial#Adjective|commercial]], [[directional]], or [[road]] [[traffic#Noun|traffic]] [[information]], taken [[collectively]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''signage''' at the airport is designed to point the way clearly to important locations.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|editor=J. F. McLaughlin|title=Proceedings of the 48th Annual Road School: Held at Purdue University, March 26–29, 1962|series=Engineering Bulletin; Engineering Extension Series (Purdue University, Department of Engineering Extension)|seriesvolume=no. 111|location=Lafayette, Ind.|publisher={{w|Purdue University}}|year=1962|page=196|oclc=24481598|passage=Uniformity must be paramount in all '''signage''' and markings and is the only sound basis from which the job of traffic control can be started on any highway system.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Bulletin|location=Detroit, Mich.|publisher=Michigan Society of Architects|year=1973|volume=48|page=51|column=2|oclc=6374206|passage=Early involvement with a '''signage''' designer can often assist the architect and the owner to identify problems in directional or informational '''signage''' that may not have been considered.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Kate W. Ragsdale, compiler|title=Effective Library Signage|series=Systems and Procedures Exchange Center Flyer|seriesvolume=208|location=[Washington, D.C.]|publisher=Office of Management Services, {{w|Association of Research Libraries}}|month=May|year=1995|page=1|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=l8DgAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA1|issn=0160-3582|oclc=60255927|passage=Perhaps no aspect of library design is as vital to the success of library users as is effective '''signage''', and certainly few other aspects are as perplexing for library planners. [...] Librarians often cannot rely on architects and interior designers to plan effective '''signage''' and must address this feature of library building design on their own.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Martin Waller|authorlink=Martin Waller|title=Jarvis chief aims to lift siege of Paris|url=http://business.timesonline.co.uk/tol/business/columnists/article807897.ece|newspaper={{w|The Times}}|location=London|publisher={{w|News UK}}|date=3 January 2003|issn=0140-0460|oclc=909100542|passage=If you try to push more and more traffic on to limited numbers of roads you require more '''signage''', more safety measures, bus lanes, cycle lanes and so on.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Jimmy Schaeffler|chapter=The Big Picture: An Overview of Digital Signage|title=Digital Signage: Software, Networks, Advertising, and Displays: A Primer for Understanding the Business|series=[[w:National Association of Broadcasters|NAB]] Executive Technology Briefings|location=Burlington, Mass.; Oxford, Oxfordshire|publisher={{w|Focal Press}}|year=2008|page=25|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=3sQ4tLf8_rgC&pg=PA25|isbn=978-0-240-81041-6|passage=[I]t is critical for today's advertisers to realize how different digital '''signage''' is today from traditional advertising, be it the difference between static '''signage''' and digital content on digital screens, on one hand, or the difference between a traditional broadcast TV ad and a digital '''signage''' ad, on the other.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Andrew Martin|title=Underground Overground: A passenger's history of the Tube|publisher=Profile Books, {{ISBN|978-1846684777}}|page=160|text=This was the beginning of the spread across the network - in station '''signage''' and also posters - of a plain and pure typeface designed for the [[Underground]] by a refined and venerated calligrapher called Edward Johnston, [...]}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Charles Husband|author2=Yunis Alam|author3=Jörg Hüttermann|author4=Joanna Fomina|chapter=Walking Manningham: Streetscapes, Soundscapes and the Semiotics of the Physical Environment|title=Lived Diversities: Space, Place and Identities in the Multi-ethnic City|location=Bristol; Chicago, Ill.|publisher={{w|Policy Press}}|year=2016|page=66|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=TLiwBAAAQBAJ&pg=PA66|isbn=978-1-4473-1571-1|passage=Passing through Manningham, whether on foot or by car, there is one aspect of the streetscape that would signal that you are in an area that is, in British terms, 'multi-ethnic', and that is the '''signage''' above the shops. [...] [T]here is also specific '''signage''' signalling the Muslim nature of some of the properties. '''Signage''', pointing out that this is a Muslim bookshop or that this is a ''halal'' butcher, indicates the religious identities that are the primary target of these shops.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|chiefly|India|elsewhere regarded as|_|nonstandard}} A sign, a [[signboard]].
#* {{quote-book|en|chapter=Institutional, Governance and Policy Framework for Tourism Development in the Islands|title=Rethink Tourism in the Andamans: Towards Building a Base for Sustainable Tourism|location=Bangalore, Karnataka|publisher=EQUATIONS &#91;{{w|Equitable Tourism Options}}&#93;|month=June|year=2008|section=section 5.1.2.2 (Department of Environment and Forests)|page=78|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=A-PbATrDntYC&pg=PA78|isbn=|passage=[T]he department is basically involved in providing basic amenities and the minimum requirements such as clearing trekking tracks, providing '''signages''', basic accommodation or tents and so on.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=K. V. S. Madaan|chapter=Store Layout, Design and Visual Merchandising|title=Fundamentals of Retailing|series=Retail Education|location=New Delhi|publisher=[[w:McGraw-Hill Education|Tata McGraw Hill Education]]|year=2009|page=203|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=Kvslirj1X08C&pg=PA203|isbn=978-0-07-009149-8|passage=External '''signages''' invite customers from different distances. Main '''signage''' makes appeal to customers approaching store from a distance of 170–180 feet, and the storefront '''signages''' makes impact from a distance of 60–70 feet.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Swati Bhalla|author2=Anuraag S.|chapter=Part 2: Display Basics|title=Visual Merchandising|series=Retail Education|location=New Delhi|publisher=[[w:McGraw-Hill Education|Tata McGraw Hill Education]]|year=2010|page=44|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=YQofM2t82HIC&pg=PA44|isbn=978-0-07-015321-9|passage=From 'parking' to 'exit' or 'washrooms' to 'please pay here'&nbsp;– a '''signage''' is at every retail point.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=J. L. Dobias|title=Cripple Mode: Hot Electric|location=[Bloomington, Ind.]|publisher={{w|Xlibris}}|year=2012|page=612|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=KStSAAAAQBAJ&pg=PA612|isbn=978-1-4691-6981-1|passage=We arrive at a place which has a '''signage''' with archaic lettering. It says "Twenty Thousand Leagues," and in simple lettering below, it says "Fine dining."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Madhu Gurung|chapter=Bajai|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=BpJQDAAAQBAJ&pg=PT22|title=The Keeper of Memories|location=Noida, India|publisher=[[w:HarperCollins|HarperCollins Publishers]]|year=2016|isbn=9789351775492|passage=When he was old enough to read, he saw '''signages''' outside beautiful buildings: 'Indians and dogs not allowed.'}}

